                                    Imports and Package
These imports bring in necessary classes for GUI (Graphical User Interface) and events handling.
  java.awt.event.* is for handling user actions like button clicks.
  java.util.* includes utilities like Map and HashMap for storing currency conversion rates.
  javax.swing.* is for creating the user interface components like buttons, text fields, and drop-down menus.

                            Storing Currency Conversion Rates
Map<String, Double> conversionRates = new HashMap<>();
conversionRates.put("Albanian Lek", 89.24);
conversionRates.put("United States Dollar", 1.0); 
...

A Map (HashMap) is used to store key-value pairs where the key is the currency name (e.g., "Albanian Lek") and the 
value is its conversion rate relative to the base currency (USD, which has a rate of 1.0).

                            Creating the GUI Components
JComboBox<String> fromCurrency = new JComboBox<>(currencies);
JComboBox<String> toCurrency = new JComboBox<>(currencies);
JTextField amountField = new JTextField();
JButton swapButton = new JButton("Swap");
...
The program creates a graphical interface with various components like:
  Drop-down menus (JComboBox) for selecting the currencies.
  A text field (JTextField) to enter the amount to convert.
  Buttons (JButton) for swapping currencies, clearing inputs, and showing transaction history.

                    Handling Button Actions (Event Listeners)
swapButton.addActionListener(new ActionListener() {
    @Override
    public void actionPerformed(ActionEvent e) {
        // Swap the selected currencies
        fromCurrency.setSelectedItem(toCurrency.getSelectedItem());
        toCurrency.setSelectedItem(fromCurrency.getSelectedItem());
    }
});

ActionListener is an interface that listens for action events, such as a button press.
The actionPerformed method is automatically called whenever the user clicks the Swap button.


